      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>UK food businesses need a food safety system based on HACCP. The law is Regulation (EC) 852/2004 and the Food Safety Act 1990.</li><li>Safer Food Better Business (SFBB) is the Food Standards Agency's pack for small businesses in England and Wales. Scotland has CookSafe.</li><li>An Environmental Health Officer expects daily records: temperature, cleaning, allergens, opening and closing.</li><li>Records help show due diligence (Food Safety Act 1990, section 21). They also drive the confidence-in-management part of the Food Hygiene Rating (England, Wales and Northern Ireland).</li><li>£75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts.</li><li>The app does not make the kitchen safe. Good records help you show due diligence.</li></ul>"
