      "html": "<p>Regulation (EC) 852/2004 article 5, as it applies in the UK, requires a permanent procedure based on the HACCP principles, with records commensurate with the nature and size of the business. Food Safety Act 1990 section 21 provides the due diligence defence. The FSA says the Food Hygiene Rating assesses how food is handled, the condition of the premises and how food safety is managed, including confidence in management. That scheme runs in England, Wales and Northern Ireland. The FSA gives the standard cooking advice as a core temperature of 70C for 2 minutes, or an equivalent such as 75C for 30 seconds. PPDS food must carry a full ingredients list with allergens emphasised from 1 October 2021. Official sources checked on 18 November 2026.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/eur/2004/852/article/5\" rel=\"noopener\">Regulation (EC) 852/2004, article 5: HACCP (legislation.gov.uk)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1990/16/section/21\" rel=\"noopener\">Food Safety Act 1990, section 21: due diligence (legislation.gov.uk)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2013/2996/schedule/4\" rel=\"noopener\">Food Hygiene (England) Regulations 2013, schedule 4: temperature control (legislation.gov.uk)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/food-hygiene-businesses/cooking\" rel=\"noopener\">Cooking food safely (gov.uk)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/introduction-to-allergen-labelling-changes-ppds\" rel=\"noopener\">Allergen labelling for PPDS food (FSA)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-hygiene-rating-scheme-fhrs-guidance-for-businesses/food-hygiene-rating-scheme-fhrs-guidance-for-businesses\" rel=\"noopener\">Food Hygiene Rating Scheme guidance for businesses (FSA, gov.uk)</a></li></ul>"
